Takes a list of binary feature files.
Feature file format: 4 byte integer followed by 4 byte floats in
sets of 13 (all in sequence). Trainclass.c is hardcoded for
13 dimensional feature vectors. Uses difference vectors. See code
for further information.

To compile, give
gcc -o trainclass *.c -lm

usage example: trainclass speechlist_forclassifier 32 16kspeech.32gau

sample of speechlist_forclassifier:

train2_set1/speech/g03a10_unpr.sph.ch1_10651_10763.13kltonly 1 113
train2_set1/speech/g03a10_unpr.sph.ch1_10891_11059.13kltonly 1 169
train2_set1/speech/g03a10_unpr.sph.ch1_11221_11499.13kltonly 1 279
train2_set1/speech/g03a10_unpr.sph.ch1_11673_11731.13kltonly 1 59
train2_set1/speech/g03a10_unpr.sph.ch1_13167_13399.13kltonly 1 233
train2_set1/speech/g03a10_unpr.sph.ch1_13570_13643.13kltonly 1 74 
